==============================================================================
B. THE COST, timed stage by stage on the real stack
==============================================================================

   ROI 512x512, 62 frames
   decode                      31.300 s   UNCHANGED by verify
   focus fields (per frame)     0.562 s   UNCHANGED by verify
   merge, full stack            0.072 s
   merge, two halves            0.103 s   (1.439 x the full merge)
   sigpow evaluation           0.0318 s   (two 512^2 FFTs)

   baseline pipeline           31.934 s
   with --verify               32.069 s
   MARGINAL COST                0.135 s  = 0.4% of the baseline

   MEASURED: the marginal cost is NOT 2x.  Decode and the focus
   fields dominate and neither is repeated; only the accumulation
   runs again, over the same total number of frames.

   EXTRAPOLATION (DERIVED, not measured): the full green quad plane
   is 3514x2344/4 = 2.059e+06 px against this ROI's
   2.621e+05.  Accumulation is linear in pixels, so the extra
   merge scales by 7.9x to 0.8 s.  sigpow does NOT scale with the
   plane: it is evaluated on one square ROI of fixed size, so it
   stays at 0.0318 s.

